# PFDS HAMT: repair colliding-key updates and nested traversal (#508).
#
# Owner-approved correctness exception, 2026-09-27; see README.md. This is an
# upstream repair, not a portability rewrite. The pinned source loses both
# keys after inserting 1 and 33, loses a third equal-hash key, and raises
# while mapping or folding nested nodes on both Patina backends, Chibi 0.12
# and Gauche 0.9.15. The original 22-check driver passed only 9 on all four.
#
# Consume five-bit hash slices once, use the PFDS bit predicate's argument
# order, retain full collision hashes, and translate bitmap positions to
# compact vector indices. Remove empty children using the shortened vector.
# Traverse the actual child node and propagate the fold callback recursively.
#
# All four implementations pass the 23-check smoke driver after correction,
# including 480 mixed operations checked against an independent alist model
# with five hash functions. Pristine compat/vendor/ extractions are unchanged.
